<%# locals: (person:) %>
<%# The two ways to fix a timesheet entry that is NOT the current shift.
    Grouped and placed below the current-shift actions on purpose: the section
    is titled "End The Shift", and leading with the rarest paths made the
    operator sort five similar-sounding correction actions before reaching the
    one they came for. Splitting on which entry each acts on is the distinction
    that actually decides the choice, so it is the one stated in the copy.

    Must render OUTSIDE #hq-verification — render_verification_update replaces
    that div wholesale on every verify, which would wipe this block. %>
<div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-base-300">
  <h3 class="heading-title text-heading mb-1">A Different Timesheet Entry</h3>
  <p class="mb-3">Neither of these touches the current shift.</p>
  <div class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row lg:items-start lg:justify-between gap-3">
    <p>
      <strong>The entry exists but is wrong.</strong> If it is not in the review list above,
      use <%= link_to "Timesheet / Corrections", person_timesheets_path(person) %>.
    </p>
    <div class="lg:text-end lg:shrink-0">
      <%= button_link "Add Missing Timesheet Request", :secondary,
                      hq_shift_manage_new_missing_request_path(person, **shift_context),
                      icon: "plus", icon_type: :solid,
                      data: { turbo_stream: true } %>
      <p class="text-stone-muted mt-1">There is no entry for the shift.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
